WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.931
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.231 --> 00:00:09.849
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:16.575
Unit fourteen: Compare and Contrast. Today you will write about similarities and differences clearly.

4
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.690
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:23.831
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:25.650
Compare.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.824
Compare means to show similarities.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.056
Compare the two systems.

9
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.349
Your turn. Say: Compare.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.131
Compare.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.803
Contrast.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:42.956
Contrast means to show differences.

13
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.283
Contrast the two plans.

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:48.570
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

15
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:52.539
Contrast.

16
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.238
Similar.

17
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.284
Similar means almost the same.

18
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.302
The two are similar.

19
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:02.267
Your turn. Say: Similar.

20
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.053
Similar.

21
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:07.725
Whereas.

22
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.053
Whereas means used to show a difference.

23
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.568
One is old, whereas one is new.

24
00:01:14.183 --> 00:01:16.870
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

25
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:20.839
Whereas.

26
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.317
Both.

27
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:25.049
Both means the two together.

28
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.895
Both have strengths.

29
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:29.578
Your turn. Say: Both.

30
00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:33.121
Both.

31
00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:34.815
Unlike.

32
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:37.387
Unlike means not like.

33
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:39.820
Unlike cars, bikes are cheap.

34
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:43.232
Your turn. Say: Unlike.

35
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.091
Unlike.

36
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.781
Difference.

37
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:52.212
Difference means a way things are not the same.

38
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.201
Name one difference.

39
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:57.272
Your turn. Say: Difference.

40
00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.134
Difference.

41
00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:02.989
Similarly.

42
00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:06.111
Similarly means in the same way.

43
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:08.600
Similarly, both are cheap.

44
00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:11.683
Your turn. Say: Similarly.

45
00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.639
Similarly.

46
00:02:16.433 --> 00:02:20.154
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.017 --> 00:02:23.585
Visal, how do I compare two things?

48
00:02:24.683 --> 00:02:36.090
List similarities and differences first. Then use words such as both, similarly and in the same way for similarities and whereas, unlike and however for differences.

49
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:38.974
How do I organise the essay?

50
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:51.986
You can write by block, describing one topic fully and then the other, or point by point, comparing both on one feature at a time.

51
00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.201
Which is better?

52
00:02:55.317 --> 00:03:06.932
Point by point is clearer for longer texts because the reader sees each comparison directly. Finish with a conclusion that states which is stronger and why.

53
00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.451
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.317 --> 00:03:12.815
Grammar focus: Comparison linkers.

55
00:03:13.115 --> 00:03:14.349
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.688
Both buses and trains are public transport.

57
00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:21.570
Trains are fast, whereas buses are cheaper.

58
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:29.797
Use both and similarly for similarities. Use whereas, while and unlike for differences. Put a comma after however.

59
00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.212
Be careful! Don't say: Both is public transport.

60
00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.491
Say: Both are public transport.

61
00:03:38.791 --> 00:03:39.978
Both takes are.

62
00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.628
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:45.887
Two Ways to Travel.

64
00:03:46.187 --> 00:03:48.930
Rithy compares buses and trains for his essay.

65
00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:52.850
Both are public transport and both reduce traffic.

66
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.435
Trains are fast, whereas buses are cheaper.

67
00:03:57.433 --> 00:04:00.594
Unlike trains, buses can reach small villages.

68
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.959
He concludes that each suits a different journey.

69
00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:09.115
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.462
Compare shows blank.

71
00:04:11.762 --> 00:04:15.810
A, only prices. B, nothing. C, similarities.

72
00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.923
The answer is C: similarities.

73
00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:24.537
Whereas shows a blank.

74
00:04:24.837 --> 00:04:27.887
A, difference. B, date. C, name.

75
00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:33.363
The answer is A: difference.

76
00:04:34.517 --> 00:04:36.191
Both means the blank together.

77
00:04:36.491 --> 00:04:39.274
A, none. B, two. C, ten.

78
00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:44.427
The answer is B: two.

79
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:47.594
Similarly means in the same blank.

80
00:04:47.894 --> 00:04:50.851
A, room. B, year. C, way.

81
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.283
The answer is C: way.

82
00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.695
What is cheaper?

83
00:04:58.995 --> 00:05:02.381
A, buses. B, trains. C, planes.

84
00:05:05.933 --> 00:05:08.165
The answer is A: buses.

85
00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.785
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.487
How do you compare two things?

87
00:05:24.283 --> 00:05:25.795
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.095 --> 00:05:39.339
I list the similarities and differences first. I use both and similarly for similarities and whereas and unlike for differences. I organise the essay point by point and end with a conclusion.

89
00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.325
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:42.217 --> 00:05:46.367
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparison linkers.

91
00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:51.618
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

92
00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:54.686
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:54.986 --> 00:05:57.731
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

